Lina (docs): Heads up — opening a PR to migrate the old curl examples in /guides/error-handling to streaming SDK snippets and add explicit 429/timeouts fallback examples. Draft: https://go/repo/drafts/stream-429-samples :wave
Ash (eng-runtime): Nice. A couple runtime notes we should call out in the samples: 1) continuous batching means you might get partial tokens before a 429, so show how to surface partial output; 2) show a lightweight batch_size config for Dedicated vs Hosted.
Kevin (sdk): Paste the curl blob and I'll produce Node + Python streaming examples with a small onRateLimit callback. Also can add a compact fallback snippet that switches to a smaller model on 429.
Lina (docs): Curl snippet is the one on the current page, small example: ```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/chat \n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $KEY\" \n  -d '{\"model\":\"redwood-1\", \"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"summarize this long doc\"}] }'
```
Kevin (sdk): Cool. Here's a very short Node pattern I can add to the PR (will redact keys): ```
const client = new RedwoodSDK({ apiKey: process.env.KEY })
try {
  for await (const chunk of client.chat.stream({ model: 'redwood-1', messages })) {
    process.stdout.write(chunk.delta)
  }
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 'rate_limit') {
    // fallback: request a compact model for faster, cheaper completion
    const compact = await client.chat.create({ model: 'redwood-compact-1', messages })
    console.log('\n[FALLBACK] partial content:', compact.output)
  } else throw err
}
```
Mark (support): We have a customer repro where bursts from their webhook cause repeated 429s after ~30s of sustained traffic. I can sanitize their request pattern and drop it into the PR as an "operator's repro" section. Useful to show how backoff + fallback reduces error rate.
Ash (eng-runtime): Also request that docs replace the internal pointer to the old playbook at /incidents/429-playbook — that link is stale. New canonical runbook is /runbooks/rate-limit. Add a tiny note about testing on Dedicated vs Hosted because autoscaling semantics differ.
Lina (docs): Good catch on links — I'll sweep all references. Action items: Kevin — add Node+Python streaming + fallback snippets; Ash — runtime note and short table summarizing behavior; Mark — sanitized customer repro; Lina — PR, update links, add a "how to test" section with a small curl load generator example. ETA end of day tomorrow? :spiral_calendar: 
Kevin (sdk): Yep, I'll push a branch with both snippets and a unit test for the fallback path. Will use an env var to force a 429 in CI for the test.
